☐  Setup
    ☐ Repo root structure (all files at the root)
    ☐ .gitignore (__pycache__, .mypy_cache, venv)
    ☐ venv + requirements.txt
    ☐ Folders: src/ tests/ docs/
    ☐ Read Chapter II (AI Instructions, pages 3-4 of the PDF)

☐  Makefile
    ☐ install
    ☐ run
    ☐ debug (pdb)
    ☐ clean (__pycache__, .mypy_cache)
    ☐ lint
        ☐ flake8 .
        ☐ mypy . --warn-return-any --warn-unused-ignores --ignore-missing-imports --disallow-untyped-defs --check-untyped-defs
    ☐ lint-strict (optional): flake8 . + mypy . --strict

☐  Parser
    ☐ Abstract class to handle the basic input
    ☐ Read file with context manager
    ☐ Ignore comments (#) and empty lines
    ☐ nb_drones
        ☐ First line of the file
        ☐ Positive integer
    ☐ Zones (start_hub / end_hub / hub)
        ☐ Exactly 1 start_hub and 1 end_hub
        ☐ Unique name, no dashes, no spaces
        ☐ Integer coordinates
    ☐ Zone metadata
        ☐ zone: normal / blocked / restricted / priority (default normal)
        ☐ Invalid zone type = parsing error
        ☐ color: any single word (default none)
        ☐ max_drones: positive integer (default 1)
        ☐ max_drones ignored on start/end (not an error)
        ☐ Tags in any order, valid bracket syntax
    ☐ Connections
        ☐ Only between previously defined zones
        ☐ Bidirectional
        ☐ No duplicates (a-b == b-a)
        ☐ max_link_capacity: positive integer (default 1)
    ☐ Errors
        ☐ Stop the program with a clear message (line + cause)
        ☐ Never crash on bad input
    ☐ Unsolvable map (no path start→end) detected and reported, no crash, no infinite loop

☐  Models (all OOP)
    ☐ Zone (type, capacity, color, coordinates, occupancy)
    ☐ Connection (zones, link capacity, occupancy)
    ☐ Graph (adjacency, no graph libs)
    ☐ Drone (id, position, state, in transit)
    ☐ Decide which class does what (parser / pathfinder / simulation / visualizer)

☐  Simulation engine
    ☐ Discrete turns
    ☐ All moves decided from the state at the start of the turn
    ☐ Zone capacity (start and end unlimited)
    ☐ Connection capacity
    ☐ Space vacated this turn is usable by another drone in the same turn
    ☐ Restricted zones
        ☐ Costs 2 turns
        ☐ Drone occupies the connection in transit
        ☐ Must arrive on the next turn (cannot wait on the connection)
        ☐ Connection freed on the arrival turn
    ☐ Blocked zones never entered
    ☐ Drones can stay in place (wait)
    ☐ Stop when all drones reach the end zone

☐  Pathfinding / scheduling
    ☐ Cost-aware search (normal 1, priority 1 but preferred, restricted 2)
    ☐ Exclude blocked zones
    ☐ Distribute drones across multiple paths
    ☐ Strategic waiting
    ☐ Avoid conflicts and deadlocks
    ☐ Respect max_drones and max_link_capacity
    ☐ Adapt to different map topologies
    ☐ Avoid infinite loops
    ☐ Compare results with the optimums (VII.6)

☐  Output
    ☐ One line per turn
    ☐ D<ID>-<zone> or D<ID>-<connection> (in transit)
    ☐ Space-separated movements
    ☐ Omit drones that did not move
    ☐ Delivered drones are no longer tracked
    ☐ Confirm connection name format

☐  Visual representation
    ☐ Colored terminal output and/or graphical interface
    ☐ Use the color= metadata
    ☐ Show drone movements and zone states

☐  Quality
    ☐ Python 3.10+
    ☐ Completely object-oriented
    ☐ Type hints (parameters, returns, variables)
    ☐ flake8 clean
    ☐ mypy clean
    ☐ Docstrings (PEP 257)
    ☐ try/except + context managers
    ☐ No graph libraries (networkx, graphlib, etc.)
    ☐ Own map files (edge cases, invalid inputs)
    ☐ Tests (pytest/unittest, not submitted)

☐  Benchmarks (optimum turns)
    ☐ Linear path (2 drones): 4
    ☐ Simple fork (4 drones): 4
    ☐ Basic capacity (4 drones): 4
    ☐ Dead end trap (5 drones): 8
    ☐ Circular loop (6 drones): 10
    ☐ Priority puzzle (5 drones): 6
    ☐ Maze nightmare (8 drones): 13
    ☐ Capacity hell (12 drones): 16
    ☐ Ultimate challenge (15 drones): 26
    ☐ Within 25% of optimum on every map
    ☐ Exact optimum on every map

☐  README (English)
    ☐ Description
    ☐ Instructions
    ☐ Resources (+ how AI was used)
    ☐ Algorithm choices + implementation strategy
    ☐ Visual representation docs
    ☐ Example input + expected output

☐  Bonus
    ☐ The Impossible Dream (25 drones): 43 turns

☐  Peer-review prep
    ☐ Explain the architecture and each class
    ☐ Explain the graph representation
    ☐ Explain the algorithm, why it was chosen, and its complexity
    ☐ Explain caching / recalculation and memory usage
    ☐ Explain capacities, simultaneous moves and restricted transit
    ☐ Explain how invalid input is handled
    ☐ Be ready for a live code modification
    ☐ Demo the program
